<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!--
    Deck plating for Save Our Ship 2 hulls.

    RL_ShipStructuralFloor cannot be reused for SOS2. That def is the Odyssey gravship deck: it is
    MayRequire-gated on Odyssey, it demands an inspected Building_GravEngine, and it counts towards an
    engine's substructure capacity. An SOS2 ship is a different model entirely (CompShipCachePart on
    every plating tile, a flat MapShipCells dictionary on ShipMapComp, Building_ShipBridge as owner),
    so a deck built on one has no engine to report to and no substructure budget to spend.

    Gated on SOS2's own terrain rather than on a mod name: PatchOperationFindMod compares
    ModMetaData.Name (the display name), which changes with translations and local forks, exactly the
    reason Patches/VGE_PipeRisers.xml tests the def too.

    Deliberately NOT tagged "Substructure", even when Odyssey is loaded. TerrainDef.IsSubstructure
    reads that tag, and SOS2's TerrainGrid_SetFoundation_DetachOnSubstructure postfix detaches every
    CompShipCachePart building on a cell that receives a substructure foundation
    (CompShipEngineBreakdownable.cs). Tagging this deck would therefore tear the hull off the ship the
    moment the player lays it. RimLayers recognises the deck by defName instead
    (StructuralSupport.IsDeckTerrain), which is configuration independent.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/TerrainDef[defName="FakeFloorInsideShip"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs</xpath>
      <value>
        <TerrainDef ParentName="FloorBase">
          <defName>RL_Sos2Deck</defName>
          <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/TileHull</texturePath>
          <isFoundation>true</isFoundation>
          <layerable>false</layerable>
          <edgeType>Hard</edgeType>
          <renderPrecedence>399</renderPrecedence>
          <terrainAffordanceNeeded>RL_FloorSupport</terrainAffordanceNeeded>
          <requireInspectedGravEngine>false</requireInspectedGravEngine>
          <affordances Inherit="False">
            <li>Light</li>
            <li>Medium</li>
            <li>Heavy</li>
            <li>Walkable</li>
            <li>RL_FloorSupport</li>
          </affordances>
          <statBases>
            <WorkToBuild>600</WorkToBuild>
            <Beauty>0</Beauty>
            <Cleanliness>0</Cleanliness>
            <Flammability>0</Flammability>
          </statBases>
          <costList>
            <Steel>4</Steel>
            <Plasteel>1</Plasteel>
          </costList>
          <resourcesFractionWhenDeconstructed>1</resourcesFractionWhenDeconstructed>
          <!-- SOS2 ships are built from the Ship tab; a deck belongs with the hull it extends. -->
          <designationCategory>Ship</designationCategory>
          <uiOrder>2010</uiOrder>
          <placeWorkers>
            <li>RimLayers.Structure.PlaceWorker_LayerSupport</li>
          </placeWorkers>
        </TerrainDef>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
